{"data":[{"id":"ffa36d02-8d87-4d8d-ba67-d63f86617b30","type":"activities","attributes":{"prov:wasGeneratedBy":"https://api.datacite.org/activities/ffa36d02-8d87-4d8d-ba67-d63f86617b30","prov:generatedAtTime":"2026-10-20T01:47:09Z","prov:wasDerivedFrom":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23487384","prov:wasAttributedTo":"https://api.datacite.org/repositories/cern.zenodo","action":"create","version":1,"changes":{"doi":"10.5281/ZENODO.23487384","url":"https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23487384","dates":[{"date":"2026-10-20","dateType":"Issued"}],"sizes":null,"types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"Other","resourceTypeGeneral":"Text"},"reason":null,"source":"api","titles":[{"title":"Project Sovereign Genesis: THE TRIANGULAR MAGNETOPLASMONIC VACUUM TRACTOR MANIFESTO A CERN-Inspired Paradigm for Macroscopic Remote Manipulation"}],"formats":null,"creators":[{"name":"Seagal, David Michael","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"David Michael","familyName":"Seagal","nameIdentifiers":[]}],"language":null,"subjects":[{"subject":"Core Disciplines \u0026 Physics Quantum Optoelectronics Graphene Electron Hydrodynamics Magnetoplasmonics Landau Quantization Inverse Faraday Effect (IFE) Landau Level Collapse Navier-Stokes Fluid Singularities Acoustic Graphene Plasmons (AGPs) Beam Wavefronts \u0026 Metamaterials Solenoid Light Drills Self-Healing Airy Beams Zero-Order Bessel Vectors Silicon-on-Glass Metasurfaces CVD Graphene Cavities Heterodyne Spectral Comb Triple-Helix Trajectories System Geometry \u0026 Scaling Asymmetric Triangle Formation Multi-Axial Vector Clamping Baseline Expansion Law Fluidic Gradient Steering Cross-Beam Management (XBM) Electrostatic Distance-Gating Vacuum Insulation Bias Real-Time Sensor Telemetry \u0026 Computing Asynchronous Ring Token Core Quantum-Well Infrared Photodetectors (QWIPs) Optically Pumped Magnetometers (OPMs) Biomagnetic Waveform Cancellation Predictive Telemetry Control Loops Nanosecond-Latency Distributed Computing"}],"container":null,"publisher":"Zenodo","aasm_state":"findable","regenerate":true,"content_url":null,"identifiers":[],"rights_list":[{"rights":"CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Strongly Reciprocal","rightsUri":"https://www.ohwr.org/project/cernohl/wikis/Documents/CERN-OHL-version-2","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"cern-ohl-s-2.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"}],"contributors":null,"descriptions":[{"description":"This manifesto outlines a mathematically rigorous, scalable engineering framework for a three-dimensional, multi-node vacuum tractor beam matrix capable of manipulating macroscopic payloads. By shifting away from classical macro-scale radiation pressure—which inherently scatters and pushes objects forward—this architecture treats the target as an active, wireless quantum circuit.\n\nThe system projects a multi-wavelength, heterodyne spectral comb (designated \"disco\" modulation) shaped into non-diffracting triple-helix solenoid curves and Airy profiles via ultra-thin silicon-on-glass metasurfaces. When these beams intersect at an unencapsulated CVD monolayer graphene cavity layer on the target, they exploit Landau-quantized Dirac fermions to compress the local electromagnetic field volume by 4,000×. This extreme compression triggers the Inverse Faraday Effect (IFE), generating ultra-dense, localized electronic vortices that behave as fluidic whirlpools under updated Navier-Stokes hydrodynamic formulas.\n\nSimultaneously, an asymmetric macroscopic electrostatic field establishes a distance-gate bias across the vacuum to induce Landau level collapse, tuning the target's energy steps from afar. Mechanical, backward-pulling conveyor grids are established directly within the target substrate using non-diffracting zero-order Bessel acoustic vectors carried via Acoustic Graphene Plasmons (AGPs).\n\nTo scale the architecture indefinitely without localized thermal destruction, the emitters are arranged in an Asymmetric Triangle Formation. This geometry expands the operational baseline, allows multi-axial vector clamping to neutralize target tumble, and intentionally introduces controlled electronic gradients to steer payloads through 3D space. The entire matrix is stabilized by a nanosecond-latency, distributed Asynchronous Ring Token Compute Core running real-time predictive codes fed by an integrated array of Thermal/IR radiometers, Optically Pumped Magnetometers (biomagnetism trackers), and Heterodyne Optical Phase sensors.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n ","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"landing_page":null,"version_info":"1","geo_locations":null,"only_validate":false,"related_items":null,"schema_version":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","should_validate":false,"publication_year":2026,"funding_references":null,"related_identifiers":[{"relationType":"HasVersion","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.23487385","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}]}}}],"meta":{"total":351349066,"totalPages":351349066,"page":1},"links":{"self":"https://api.datacite.org/activities?page%5Bsize%5D=1","next":"https://api.datacite.org/activities?page%5Bnumber%5D=2\u0026page%5Bsize%5D=1"}}